    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on August 26, our lineup is headlined by **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) and **Corbin Carroll** (70.87), who represent our primary avenues for stolen base production. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from an ideal matchup against the left-handed Rodriguez, and his efficiency is bolstered by the opponent's slow delivery, which significantly increases his stolen base potential. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher path against an elite hold pitcher, his elite speed remains a priority, keeping him in the green despite a slight downward adjustment for the matchup context. **Brice Turang** (69.94) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.13) also grade as elite starts; **Mickey Moniak** specifically benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Waldron, providing a high-floor opportunity to capitalize on Roto categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the marginal starters in the bottom of the lineup. **Zach McKinstry** (51.44) and **Jose Caballero** (51.19) just barely cleared the threshold for inclusion, largely due to their unique speed profiles in a landscape where steals are the scarcest commodity. **Austin Riley** (54.66) was nearly pushed out of the lineup due to his unfavorable #8 spot in the order, but his base projection remains high enough to outpace the empty bench. We are currently navigating a thin roster; with **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all unavailable due to rest or injury status, our bench is strictly defensive. We are keeping a close eye on **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot-start opportunities should any late-scratch lineup news shift our projected scores. \n\nRisk remains concentrated on the pitching side of our matchups, specifically for **Vinnie Pasquantino** (52.85), who faces a stern test against Miles. While his dynamic platoon advantage keeps him viable, the negative impact of the opposing starter's skill level creates a lower-ceiling outcome compared to the rest of our core. We have optimized for maximum volume across the board, prioritizing those with the highest speed-floor to keep us competitive in the 5x5 hunt as we navigate this mid-week stretch.",
